---
/*
 * Privacy policy, English courtesy translation of DatenschutzDe.astro
 * (binding). Operator, supervisory authority and Umami settings come from
 * src/data/legal.ts.
 */
import OperatorAddress from './OperatorAddress.astro';
import {
  ANALYTICS,
  OPERATOR,
  SUPERVISORY_AUTHORITY as authority,
} from '../../data/legal.ts';
import { CONSENT_STRINGS } from '../../i18n/consent.ts';
import { CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY } from '../../scripts/consent.ts';

const mailto = `mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`;
const cloudflarePrivacy = 'https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/';
const umamiPrivacy = 'https://umami.is/privacy';
const daily = ANALYTICS.idRotation === 'daily';
const saltChange = daily ? 'every day' : 'at the start of every calendar month';
const idPeriod = daily ? 'one day' : 'one calendar month';
const retention = `${ANALYTICS.retentionMonths} months`;
const settings = `“${CONSENT_STRINGS.en.settings}”`;
const decline = `“${CONSENT_STRINGS.en.decline}”`;
const consentKey = `“${CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY}”`;
---

<h2>1. Controller</h2>
<p>
  The controller responsible for processing personal data on this website within
  the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
</p>
<OperatorAddress language="en" />
<p>
  Email: <a href={mailto}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>
</p>

<h2>2. Summary</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    This website sets no cookies. There is no contact form, no newsletter and no
    user accounts.
  </li>
  <li>
    We use Cloudflare to deliver the website. We compile visitor statistics with
    Umami Cloud only if you consent via the banner on the website; you can
    change your decision at any time under {settings} in the footer of the
    website. Both services process your IP address; it is not stored in the
    statistics.
  </li>
  <li>
    The designs you mark with “Want” are stored only in your browser, as is your
    decision on visitor statistics.
  </li>
  <li>
    The fonts are delivered with the website. We do not embed content from other
    providers such as videos, maps or social media plugins.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Delivery of the website via Cloudflare</h2>
<p>
  This website is delivered through the Cloudflare network (Cloudflare Workers
  and content delivery network). The provider is Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend
  St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA.
</p>
<p>
  Each time you open a page, your browser sends technically necessary data to
  Cloudflare’s servers. This includes in particular:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>your IP address,</li>
  <li>the date and time of the request,</li>
  <li>the requested address (URL) and the amount of data transferred,</li>
  <li>the referrer, i.e. the page you came from, if your browser sends it,</li>
  <li>
    the information your browser sends about browser type and version, operating
    system and language setting,
  </li>
  <li>technical connection data such as protocol and status code.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  The data is processed to deliver the website, to keep it stable and secure and
  to fend off attacks. The legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate
  interest is the secure and reliable provision of the website. Only the
  information your browser sends with every request anyway is processed.
</p>
<p>
  Cloudflare processes this data on our behalf under a data processing agreement
  (Art.&nbsp;28 GDPR). Processing may take place in the USA and in other
  countries where Cloudflare operates data centres. Cloudflare is certified
  under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; transfers to the USA are therefore
  based on the European Commission’s adequacy decision of 10&nbsp;July 2023
  (Art.&nbsp;45 GDPR). For other transfers to third countries, Cloudflare has
  agreed to the EU standard contractual clauses (Art.&nbsp;46(2)(c) GDPR).
</p>
<p>
  Cloudflare keeps this data only as long as necessary for these purposes. For
  more information, see
  <a href={cloudflarePrivacy}>Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
</p>

<h2>4. Visitor statistics with Umami Cloud</h2>
<p>
  To understand which pages and designs people are interested in, we use the
  analytics service Umami Cloud. The provider is Umami Software, Inc., 28 Geary
  St, Suite 650 #243, San Francisco, California, USA.
</p>
<p>
  Only if you have consented does your browser, when you open a page, load the
  Umami script from cloud.umami.is and then send usage data to gateway.umami.is.
  Without your consent, no connection to Umami is made. The following is
  processed:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>the page you open (address and page title) and the time,</li>
  <li>the referrer, i.e. the page you came from, if your browser sends it,</li>
  <li>
    browser, operating system and device type, screen size and language setting,
  </li>
  <li>
    your approximate location (country, region, city), which Umami derives from
    your IP address,
  </li>
  <li>
    when you click “Want” on a design or remove the mark again: which design is
    concerned, which options were selected, for example shirt colour or footnote
    language, and where on the website you clicked. Marks made before you
    consented are not transmitted retroactively.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Your IP address is processed only briefly, to answer the request, determine
  the approximate location and calculate a visitor identifier; it is not stored
  in the statistics. Umami’s infrastructure providers may keep it for a limited
  time in operational and security logs. The visitor identifier is a hash of the
  IP address, the browser identification (user agent), our website’s ID and a
  secret value that Umami changes {saltChange}. It allows page views within
  {idPeriod} to be grouped; after that a new identifier is created and earlier
  page views can no longer be linked to it. Umami sets no cookies and does not
  track you across other websites.
</p>
<p>
  The script stores no information on your device. When it loads, it reads
  information your browser makes available to websites (screen size, language
  setting, address and title of the page) and checks whether the entry
  “umami.disabled”, which switches the measurement off, is set in your browser.
</p>
<p>
  We use the statistics to learn how the website is used and which designs
  people like, and to decide which designs to produce. We chose a method that
  works without cookies, without storing IP addresses and without cross-site
  identifiers. The legal basis is your consent: Art.&nbsp;6(1)(a) GDPR for the
  processing of your data and §&nbsp;25(1) of the German Telecommunications
  Digital Services Data Protection Act (TDDDG) for reading information from your
  device.
</p>
<p>
  You give your consent via the banner that appears on your first visit to the
  website. It is voluntary; if you decline, you can use the website without any
  restrictions. You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the
  future (Art.&nbsp;7(3) GDPR) by choosing {settings} in the footer of the
  website and clicking {decline}. From then on your browser sends no more data
  to Umami. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out
  before it.
</p>
<p>
  So that we do not ask you again on every page, the website stores your
  decision in your browser’s local storage under the entry {consentKey}: whether
  you accepted or declined, and when. The entry is not transmitted to us or to
  anyone else and stays stored until you change your decision or delete the data
  this website has stored in your browser. If local storage is unavailable, your
  decision applies only to the page currently open. This storage is strictly
  necessary for the website to respect your decision and therefore permitted
  without consent under §&nbsp;25(2) no.&nbsp;2 TDDDG. To the extent that
  personal data is processed, the legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR; our
  legitimate interest is to respect your decision without asking you again and
  again.
</p>
<p>
  Umami processes the data on our behalf under a data processing agreement
  (Art.&nbsp;28 GDPR). We selected the EU data region for our account, so the
  statistics are stored in the EU. However, Umami Software, Inc. is based in the
  USA and also uses sub-processors in the USA, so transfers to the USA cannot be
  ruled out. They are based on the EU standard contractual clauses
  (Art.&nbsp;46(2)(c) GDPR), which are part of the data processing agreement.
</p>
<p>
  The statistics are deleted after {retention}. Regardless of your decision in
  the banner, you can also technically prevent the measurement by blocking
  scripts from cloud.umami.is with a content blocker or by disabling JavaScript.
  For more information, see <a href={umamiPrivacy}>Umami’s privacy policy</a>.
</p>

<h2>5. “Want” marks in your browser</h2>
<p>
  When you click “Want” on a design, the website saves the list of designs you
  have marked in your browser’s local storage. This keeps your marks when you
  move between pages or come back to the website later. The list contains no
  identifier that identifies you and is not transmitted to us or to anyone else.
  If you have consented to the visitor statistics, the click itself is also
  counted there (see section&nbsp;4).
</p>
<p>
  You can remove a mark by clicking again, or delete all data this website has
  stored in your browser settings. Otherwise the list stays stored until you
  delete it.
</p>
<p>
  The list is saved only once you use the feature, and solely to provide the
  marking feature you asked for. This is strictly necessary for that feature and
  therefore permitted without consent under §&nbsp;25(2) no.&nbsp;2 TDDDG. To
  the extent that personal data is processed, the legal basis is
  Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest is to offer you the marking
  feature.
</p>

<h2>6. Contact by email</h2>
<p>
  If you send us an email, we process your email address, the content of your
  message and any other information you give us in order to answer your enquiry.
  The legal basis is Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest is
  answering your enquiry. The message is stored with our email provider. We
  delete it once your enquiry has been dealt with, unless statutory retention
  obligations require otherwise.
</p>

<h2>7. Link to Instagram</h2>
<p>
  The footer of this website links to an Instagram profile. It is a plain link:
  no data is sent to Instagram when you visit our website. Only if you follow
  the link do you go to Instagram, operated by Meta Platforms Ireland Limited,
  whose privacy policy then applies.
</p>

<h2>8. Fonts</h2>
<p>
  The fonts of this website are delivered together with the website. There is no
  connection to external font services such as Google Fonts.
</p>

<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
<p>
  Under the GDPR you have the following rights regarding personal data
  concerning you:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>access (Art.&nbsp;15 GDPR),</li>
  <li>rectification (Art.&nbsp;16 GDPR),</li>
  <li>erasure (Art.&nbsp;17 GDPR),</li>
  <li>restriction of processing (Art.&nbsp;18 GDPR),</li>
  <li>data portability (Art.&nbsp;20 GDPR),</li>
  <li>objection to processing (Art.&nbsp;21 GDPR, see below),</li>
  <li>
    withdrawal of consent with effect for the future (Art.&nbsp;7(3) GDPR); for
    the visitor statistics at any time via {settings} in the footer of the
    website.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  To exercise them, simply write to us at <a href={mailto}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>.
</p>
<p>
  The statistics and the decision stored in your browser (section&nbsp;4) and
  the marks in your browser (section&nbsp;5) contain nothing that allows us to
  identify you. We can therefore usually not match enquiries about this data to
  a person (Art.&nbsp;11 GDPR).
</p>

<h3>Right to object under Art.&nbsp;21 GDPR</h3>
<p>
  Where we process data on the basis of Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR, you have the
  right to object to this processing at any time on grounds relating to your
  particular situation. We will then no longer process the data unless we can
  demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override
  your interests, rights and freedoms, or the processing serves the
  establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
</p>

<h3>Right to lodge a complaint</h3>
<p>
  You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
  authority (Art.&nbsp;77 GDPR), in particular in the member state of your
  habitual residence, place of work or place of the alleged infringement. The
  authority responsible for us is: <a href={authority.url}>{authority.name}</a>.
</p>

<h2>10. Further information</h2>
<p>
  You are not obliged to provide us with personal data. Without the data
  transmitted technically when you open a page (section&nbsp;3), however, the
  website cannot be delivered. There is no automated decision-making, including
  profiling (Art.&nbsp;22 GDPR).
</p>
<p>
  We update this privacy policy when the website or the law changes. The version
  published here applies.
</p>
